From a710a97617b7892ee33dc85153dabeb293a93e65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fredrik Averpil <fredrik.averpil@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 16:44:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(explorer): add reviewed file markers

Reviewing a large diff means keeping track of which files have already been
looked at, which is otherwise done from memory. `v` in the explorer or history
panel marks the file under the cursor, marked rows are tinted and prefixed
with a check, and `]f`/`[f` skip them, so repeatedly pressing `]f` walks only
what is left.

The key is bound on the panel buffers only, so the diff panes keep `v` for
Visual mode (and the `vih` hunk text object).

Marks are per-tab and deliberately not persisted: the same file is worth
reviewing again in the next diff. Single-file history marks commits rather
than files, since there each commit is the unit being reviewed.

The mark bookkeeping is shared by both panels via codediff.ui.reviewed,
including the list walk that decides which row to visit next, so explorer and
history cannot drift apart on what "next unreviewed" means. Navigation keeps
upstream's positional messages while nothing is marked, and only switches to
review-aware wording once the feature is actually in use.
